# API Configuration for Ionic React + Vite
# Multi-device support: Desktop (localhost), Mobile (local IP), and ngrok

# Option 1: Use localhost (desktop development)
# VITE_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000/api

# Option 2: Use your local network IP for mobile device testing
# Find your local IP address:
#   Windows: Run 'ipconfig' in terminal (look for IPv4 Address under your network adapter)
#   Mac/Linux: Run 'ifconfig' or 'ip addr' (look for inet under your network interface)
# Then replace <YOUR_LOCAL_IP> with your actual IP (e.g., 192.168.1.100)
# VITE_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://<YOUR_LOCAL_IP>:3000/api

# Option 3: Use ngrok for external/mobile access over internet
# 1. Install ngrok: npm install -g ngrok
# 2. Start ngrok tunnel: ngrok http 3000
# 3. Copy the HTTPS URL from ngrok output
# 4. Replace <your-ngrok-subdomain> with your actual ngrok subdomain
# VITE_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://<your-ngrok-subdomain>.ngrok-free.dev/api

# App Configuration
APP_NAME=School App Ionic
APP_VERSION=1.0.0

# Notes:
# - The ngrok-skip-browser-warning header is automatically included in all API requests
# - CORS is configured to accept requests from localhost, local IPs (192.168.x.x, 10.x.x.x), and ngrok domains
# - withCredentials is enabled globally for proper session/cookie handling across origins